{
  "_comment": "EverQuest-inspired custom spell pack. Consumed by tools/build_client_patch.py, which clones a neutral native base row (Crippling Poison 25809: zero attributes, no stance/family/cooldown baggage) and applies these overrides, then emits both the client Spell.dbc rows (patch-P.mpq) and data/sql/db-world/28_eq_spell_pack.sql (dbc_spells + dbc_skilllineability rows so the draft pool can see them). Spell IDs 993001-993030 are reserved for this pack. 'value' is the in-game number; the tool stores value-1 in EffectBasePoints per DBC convention. 'draftable': false spells are hidden helpers (proc payloads) that get a Spell.dbc row but no draft-pool row. Icons/visuals are reused verbatim from existing native spells - no new art. Deliberately overtuned by design. IDs 993301-993320 are the class-tab talent sub-range (Squall Line / Storm's Edge / Gale Force / Crusading Zealot + the Crusader Strike rank clones / Crusader's Fury, see .agents/plans/melee-talent-rework/): all 'draftable': false, because they are talent rank spells in real class tabs (Talent.dbc rows 3000-3004) rather than draft-pool picks. Two extra keys exist for that sub-range: 'clone_from' copies a named native record verbatim and then applies only the keys present (so a rank clone cannot drift from its parent in an unrelated column), and an explicit 'family' (+ optional 'family_flags' on the spell, or a per-effect 'classmask' [w0, w1, w2]) targets a STOCK spell family - e.g. family 11 + classmask [0, 16, 0] is Stormstrike, family 10 + [0, 32768, 0] is Crusader Strike - where 'family_bit' targets this pack's own shared custom family instead.",
